export default async function BuildDetail({params}:{params:Promise<{id:string}>}){const {id}=await params;const build=builds.find(b=>b.id===id);if(!build)return <main className={s.page}><header className={s.mast}><Link href="/100-builds">← MAIN GALLERY</Link></header><section className={s.planned}><h1>BUILD NOT FOUND</h1></section></main>;const active=activeCopy[id]??{question:(build.public?.plainPurpose??build.description).toUpperCase(),a:`Use the working tool to explore this question: ${build.public?.plainPurpose??build.functional.summary??build.description}`,b:`Watch the build-specific film, inspect its motion argument, then use the interactive web version to test: ${build.visual.mechanism??build.description}`};const state:PublicBuildState=build.publicState??'ComingNext';
 if(state==='ComingNext')return <main className={s.page}><header className={s.mast}><Link href="/100-builds">← MAIN GALLERY</Link><span>BUILD {id} / 100 · {label[state]}</span></header><section className={s.planned}><div className={s.number}>FROZEN CANON / FUTURE CYCLE</div><h1>{build.title}</h1><p>{build.description}</p><div className={s.notes}><div><h3>A / THE THING</h3><p>{build.functional.summary}</p></div><div><h3>B / THE STORY</h3><p>{build.visual.mechanism}</p></div></div><p>This room shows where the build is headed without pretending the artifact already exists. Its working tool, interactive visual master, public record, archive and LinkedIn-native derivative enter the room when this cycle begins.</p>{build.usesInfrastructure.length>0&&<p><strong>EARLIER BUILDS IT WILL INHERIT FROM /</strong> {build.usesInfrastructure.join(' · ')}</p>}</section></main>;
 const lab=state==='InLab';const media=getLinkedInMedia(id);const hasArchive=Boolean(buildArchives[id]);const hasRecord=['001','002','003','004','005','006'].includes(id);const archiveCoverage=publicArchiveCoverageCopy(id);
 return <main className={s.page}><header className={s.mast}><Link href="/100-builds">← MAIN GALLERY</Link><span>BUILD {id} / 100 · {label[state]}</span></header><section className={s.wall}><div className={s.number}>BUILD {id}<br/>PHASE {String(build.phase).padStart(2,'0')}<br/>2026</div><div className={s.title}><h1>{build.title}</h1><p>{build.description}</p></div><aside className={s.label}>A / USE IT — WORKING PROTOTYPE<br/>B / WATCH + EXPLORE — LINKEDIN CUT → MOTION ARGUMENT → INTERACTIVE WEB MASTER<br/>B-LINKEDIN — {media?'CAPTIONED FILM + TRANSCRIPT':'NOT YET PUBLISHED'}<br/>ARCHIVE / DURABLE SYSTEM OF RECORD<br/><br/>STATUS / {label[state]}<br/>PHASE / {String(build.phase).padStart(2,'0')}<br/><br/>QUESTION / {active.question}</aside></section><section className={s.orientation} aria-label="Build orientation"><article><span>WHAT IT IS</span><p>A paired public prototype: A is the working tool; B turns the same question into a film, motion argument and interactive web experience.</p></article><article><span>WHY IT MATTERS</span><p>{build.public?.plainPurpose??build.description}</p></article><article><span>RN&apos;S ROLE</span><p>RN conceived the question, structured the research and evidence boundaries, designed the information and interaction, implemented the prototype and documented its limits.</p></article><article><span>WHAT IT CANNOT CLAIM</span><p>{build.limitations.length?build.limitations.slice(0,2).join(' '):'This independent prototype demonstrates an approach; it is not a deployed client system, professional advice or proof of real-world outcomes.'}</p></article></section>{lab&&<section className={s.labNote}><strong>WORKING PROTOTYPE</strong><p>You can use and explore this build now. Its public evidence record is still being completed, so treat the experience as a demonstration—not a certified institutional system.</p></section>}{evidenceCertifiedIds.has(id)&&<section className={s.labNote} aria-label="Evidence boundary and source status"><strong>PUBLIC EVIDENCE RECORD · CERTIFIED SCOPE</strong><p>The published record has completed its stated claim-to-source review. Certification is limited to the documented claims and sources; it does not prove effectiveness, safety, compliance, representativeness, cultural authority, professional suitability or outcomes.</p></section>}{evidenceOpenIds.has(id)&&<section className={s.labNote} aria-label="Evidence boundary and source status"><strong>CLAIM-TO-SOURCE REVIEW · HOLD / OPEN</strong><p>Retained archive sources may exist, but public claim-to-source certification remains open. Overview, A, B, film, captions and downloadable transcript are a synthetic design fixture, not evidence of effectiveness, safety, compliance, representativeness, cultural authority, professional suitability or outcomes.</p></section>}{claimReview[id]&&<section className={s.labNote} aria-label="Claim review and source limits"><strong>{lateReviewPending.has(id)?'REMEDIATED PUBLIC CLAIMS · HOLD — INDEPENDENT POST-FIX REVIEW PENDING':(claimReview[id].label??'CLAIM-TO-SOURCE REVIEW · HOLD')}</strong><p><b>Source:</b> {claimReview[id].source}. {claimReviewLinks[id]?.map(link=><span key={link.url}> <a href={link.url} rel="noreferrer">{link.label}</a>.</span>)} <b>Exact locator:</b> {claimReview[id].locator}. <b>Limit:</b> {claimReview[id].limit} This status does not validate real-world effectiveness, safety, compliance, representativeness, cultural authority, professional suitability, or outcomes.</p></section>}<section className={s.objects}><Link className={s.object} href={`/100-builds/${id}/a`}><span>{id}-A / THE THING</span><h2>Use it</h2><p>{active.a}</p><b>OPEN THE TOOL →</b></Link><Link className={s.object} href={`/100-builds/${id}/b`}><span>{id}-B / THE STORY</span><h2>Watch + explore it</h2><p>{active.b}</p><b>ENTER THE VISUAL BUILD →</b></Link></section><section className={s.publicLayers}><div className={s.layerIntro}><span>THE WORK BEHIND THE ARTIFACT</span><h2>The build is more than the interface.</h2><p>Research, planning, evidence, rejected approaches, technical decisions, audits, media, source paths and forward dependencies are retained as part of the build—not left behind in conversation history.</p></div><div className={s.layerGrid}>{hasArchive?<Link href={`/100-builds/${id}/archive`}><span>{archiveCoverage.label}</span><strong>{archiveCoverage.title}</strong><p>{archiveCoverage.detail}</p></Link>:<article className={s.unavailableLayer}><span>{archiveCoverage.label}</span><strong>{archiveCoverage.title}</strong><p>{archiveCoverage.detail}</p></article>}{hasRecord?<Link aria-label="Open the public build record" href={`/100-builds/${id}/record`}><span>PUBLIC BUILD RECORD</span><strong>Making + method + evidence + limits</strong><p>The concise visitor-facing account of what changed and what it cannot claim.</p></Link>:<article className={s.unavailableLayer}><span>PUBLIC BUILD RECORD · NOT YET CERTIFIED</span><strong>Evidence and limitations review remains open</strong><p>No public record is linked until its making, method, evidence and limitations sections are complete.</p></article>}{id==='001'&&<Link href="/100-builds/001/evidence"><span>DEEP EVIDENCE</span><strong>Claim-to-source provenance</strong><p>Exact primary sources, relevant sections, freshness notes and source-vs-heuristic distinctions.</p></Link>}<Link href="/lineage"><span>LINEAGE</span><strong>What this build inherits and leaves behind</strong><p>Concrete capabilities—not thematic similarity—power the compounding sequence.</p></Link><Link href="/100-builds/archive"><span>PROGRAM ARCHIVE</span><strong>How this cycle fits the whole 100</strong><p>Syllabus, feasibility audit, strategic-value audit, canonical audit, release standard, design system and archive policy.</p></Link>{media?<a href={media.path} download={`build-${id}-linkedin.mp4`}><span>B-LINKEDIN / DOWNLOAD</span><strong>Take the 4:5 film</strong><p>{media.width}×{media.height} · {media.fps} fps · {media.durationSeconds}s · silent-first</p></a>:archiveCoverage.available?<Link href={`/100-builds/${id}/archive`}><span>B-LINKEDIN / MEDIA RECORD</span><strong>Film production record</strong><p>No canonical film has been generated for this cycle yet.</p></Link>:<article className={s.unavailableLayer}><span>B-LINKEDIN / NOT PUBLISHED</span><strong>No verified media file is available</strong><p>The page does not offer a download or archive link until a canonical file and public record exist.</p></article>}</div></section><nav className={s.sequence} aria-label="Build sequence">{Number(id)>1?<Link href={`/100-builds/${String(Number(id)-1).padStart(3,'0')}`}>← Previous build</Link>:<Link href="/100-builds">← Main gallery</Link>}<Link href="/100-builds">Find another path</Link>{Number(id)<100?<Link href={`/100-builds/${String(Number(id)+1).padStart(3,'0')}`}>Next build →</Link>:<Link href="/lineage">See the complete lineage →</Link>}</nav><section className={s.notes}><div><h3>What this build is testing</h3><p>{build.description}</p></div><div><h3>What it leaves behind</h3><p>{build.createsInfrastructure.join(' · ')}</p></div></section></main>}
